# Copy to .env.local and fill in. All optional — the app runs without them.

# ─── Supabase (account sync, PRD §5.7) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Both optional. Leave them unset and the app runs local-only: everything works
# except signing in, and the YOU screen says sync isn't configured rather than
# offering a button that fails. Dexie/IndexedDB is the store either way.
#
# Find these in your Supabase project under Settings → API.
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the **anon / publishable** key. It is public by
#   design and ships in the client bundle — row-level security is what protects
#   user data, not this key (see supabase/schema.sql).
#
#   Either key format works. New projects issue `sb_publishable_…`; older ones
#   show a legacy `anon` JWT starting `eyJ…`. Nothing here parses the key, so
#   both are passed through to the SDK untouched.
#
#   NEVER put the service_role key here, or in any VITE_-prefixed variable.
#   Vite inlines VITE_* into the client bundle, so that would publish a key
#   which bypasses every RLS policy to anyone who opens devtools.
#
# Run supabase/schema.sql against the project once before signing in, or the
# first sync fails on missing tables.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
